Statement that would follow (V11-2 (a), (b) with E-v11-1, E-v11-2; Theorem B): there is a stationary solution h = h_* + k of the 013 profile problem with k real and S1, k in K(R_*, M) inside B(Rbar, M): ||k||_2 <= R_* <= 0.000000454926094679 <= Rbar = 17/8750000 and ||J^(21/10)(W k)||_2 <= M (M = 387/1000 in the plan-of-record cell, M <= 1/2); L_* + U[k].grad has the full L^2 inverse of T2.7 with rate beta_0* >= 7/4 and the weighted estimate of V11-2 (a); and <X> h is in C^(1,1/10)(R^2) (V11-2 (b)). V11-2 (d) stays OPEN.
